  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat oven to 450 degrees F (230 degrees C).",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Combine baking mix, milk and cheddar cheese in mixing bowl. Beat with wooden spoon till soft dough forms.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Drop dough by spoonfuls onto ungreased cookie sheet. Bake 8-10 minutes until golden brown.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Mix butter and garlic powder and brush over warm biscuits before removing from cookie sheet.",
      "group": null
    }
  ],
  "footnotes": [],
  "nutrition": null,
  "importedNotes": [
    {
      "text": "I doubled the cheese and used the extra aged super sharp cheddar. I mixed the garlic in with the Bisquik & cheese, and then I put parsley and more garlic in the butter and brushed it on both before and after baking."
    },
    {
      "text": "I melted 1/4 cup butter, added 1/4 tsp garlic powder, dash of salt, and dried parsley flakes, and I used a sharp cheddar cheese."
    },
    {
      "text": "I make smaller biscuits, they cook all the way through and tend not to burn (we get a dozen from the recipe)."
    }
